## 6. Experimental Results

The KNWM work includes a set of controlled experiments designed to evaluate knowledge learning, compositional reasoning, prediction, and planning.

### Complex Physics Problem-Solving

Result: 82 / 93

KNWM solved 82 of 93 selected physics problems under controlled evaluation conditions.

### Compositional Reasoning

Result: 300 / 300

KNWM successfully completed 300 controlled multi-step knowledge composition tasks.

### Planning Performance

Result: 17 vs. 6 optimal plans out of 24 tasks

With validated knowledge reuse, KNWM produced more optimal plans than the condition without such reuse.

### Scientific Law Learning

Result: 40 / 40

The system successfully learned 40 scientific relationships in the evaluation setting.

### Trajectory Prediction

Result: 6,000 / 6,000 checkpoints

KNWM completed 6,000 prediction checkpoints across 200 evaluated trajectories under the provided motion laws.

These results support the feasibility of the architecture under structured experimental settings, while also clarifying the limits of the current evaluation framework.

