## 7. Current Research Extensions

I am continuing to extend KNWM in multiple directions.

### LLM–KNWM Integration

I developed an initial AGI-oriented system that combines KNWM with an LLM.

In this architecture:

- the LLM mainly handles language input and output
- KNWM handles knowledge, memory, reasoning, and planning

This provides an initial mechanism for capability expansion, where KNWM can identify missing capabilities, guide code creation, test the result, and retain newly learned capabilities for future use.

### 3D Perception

I am also exploring ways to connect KNWM with 3D visual perception so that structured observations can be integrated into the knowledge system.

### Embodied Planning

Another direction is to apply KNWM to embodied intelligence and adaptive planning under changing environmental conditions.

These are ongoing research directions, not claims of fully deployed real-world robotic systems.

